1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,419
Boss texts two words

2
00:00:01,499 --> 00:00:02,724
“hey” then goes silent.

3
00:00:02,803 --> 00:00:04,697
Checked five times in ten minutes.

4
00:00:05,206 --> 00:00:06,516
Not just that one day.

5
00:00:06,916 --> 00:00:09,900
Red dot pops, hand grabs phone.

6
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:14,990
Exhausted at night, blaming my focus.

7
00:00:15,691 --> 00:00:16,874
Even muting alerts fails.

8
00:00:17,274 --> 00:00:21,024
I still peek, fearing missed pings.

9
00:00:21,423 --> 00:00:25,131
Faster work, or just more stress?

10
00:00:25,832 --> 00:00:28,519
Kushlev 2015 tested this on email:

11
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:34,414
3 checks vs over 15: less stress.

12
00:00:35,115 --> 00:00:37,440
Emails received and replied stayed identical.

13
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:43,723
Instant relief. Just constant switching.

14
00:00:44,423 --> 00:00:47,810
New rule: tell your team to call.

15
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:54,640
Batch messages at 9, 1, and 4.

16
00:00:55,341 --> 00:00:58,021
Just my workaround; every job differs.

17
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,731
Anyone else glued to red dots?

18
00:01:01,131 --> 00:01:05,069
How do you handle it? Tell me.
